# TypeScript style

## Imports

```typescript
// ✅ Server (NodeNext ESM) — relative + .js extension
import { isAppError } from '../shared/http/errors.js';

// ✅ Client — relative, no path alias
import { fetchJson } from '../api/http';

// ❌ Do not invent @/ aliases or omit .js on server imports
```

## Naming

| Area | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Server files/folders | kebab-case + role suffix | `app-settings.service.ts` |
| Server suffixes | `.routes` `.schema` `.service` `.repository` `.types` `.file-store` | `prompts.routes.ts` |
| Client pages | PascalCase | `PromptsPage.tsx` |
| Client API modules | camelCase | `appSettings.ts` |
| Component dirs | kebab-case | `components/prompts/` |

## Types

- Prefer `unknown` + narrowing over `any`.
- Reuse domain types from `*.types.ts` or Zod `z.infer<>` — do not redefine parallel interfaces for the same payload.
